\par\par \b \uc2  Plaza accord lives on, top bankers agree in Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoko Kobayashi \par \uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 24 (Reuter) - Central bankers and top financial officials from countries that sealed a major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accord 10 years ago reaffirmed in Tokyo on Tuesday the importance of international coordination for stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "The spirit of Plaza has lived on and grown into the international economic coordination that today exists within the G7 (Group of Seven industrialised countries) and IMF (International Monetary Fund)," Daniel Lebegue, former head of the French Treasury, told a two-day symposium in Tokyo to commemorate the 10th anniversary of the Plaza Agreement. \par \par \uc2  The agreement, reached in 1985, was an effort by the Group of Five nations (Britain, France, Germany, Japan and the United States) to seek the depreciation of the so-called "superdollar", whose sharp rise during 1984 and 1985 threatened world financial stability. \par \par \uc2  The aggrement, named after the hotel in New York at which the meeting took place, was seen as a landmark in coordination among major industrial nations, calling for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by world central banks to weaken the dollar and urging coordination in fiscal and economic policies to correct external imbalances. \par \par \uc2  The coordinated efforts among major nations continued on up to the Louvre Accord of 1987, at which they agreed to prop up the dollar after a prolonged fall. \par \par \uc2  By the end of 1988, however, enthusiasm for international cooperation lost momentum as nations turned their eyes to domestic matters when making economic policy, which sometimes went against the interests of the world economy. \par \par \uc2  Still, the Plaza Agreement ended a period regarded as "benign neglect" in which monetary authorities left the markets untouched, and introduced a concept of subtle policy coordination and monetary cooperation, French \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Jean-Claude Trichet told the symposium. \par \par \uc2  "This is particularly true in the field of the signals that are sent to the market by means of agreed language or by means of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Trichet said. \par \par \uc2  Several rounds of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the G7, which consists of the G5 plus Canada and Italy, to prop up the sagging dollar over the past year were resounding failures until a G7 declaration in April which expressed determination to seek "an orderly reversal" of the weak dollar. \par \par \uc2  The move reassured markets and enabled successful joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August which helped the dollar rebound to around 100 yen from a record low of 79.75 yen in April. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank board member Gerd Haeusler said coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may work well if it goes along with market trends. \par \par \uc2  "Successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs favourable market conditions, that is, at least some vulnerable speculators with lopsided positions," Haeusler said. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Yasuo Matsushita said joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an effective means in the short term for correcting market misperceptions about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements and removing uncertainties. \par \par \uc2  But in the long run, countries need to adopt macroeconomic discipline to achieve sustained, non-inflationary growth and address widening external imbalances, to give their coordinated efforts credibility stemming from economic fundamentals, central bankers and former financial officials said. \par \par \uc2  In coordinating macroeconomic policies, major countries must pursue well-balanced policy mixes. Fiscal policies are often dominated by domestic factors and questions remain as to what degree monetary policies will balance this out internationally. It is also a question as to which countries should shoulder the burden of adapting polices, Haeusler said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drao02qe5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
