\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Baker/Intl Coordination -2: Against Capital Controls \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 1995\par 11:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Without U.S. leadership, successes like the Plaza and Louvre accords will remain the exception, not the rule, said former U.S. Secretary of the Treasury Baker. \par \par \uc2  In 1985, under the Plaza Accord, finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of the U.S., Germany, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , France and the U.K. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in concert to bolster the value of the major non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar. At the same time, the G-5 also agreed to pursue more closely coordinated fiscal and monetary policies. \par \par \uc2  Coordinated G-5 efforts under the the Louvre Accord of February 1987 helped maintain exchange rates at their 'then-current levels' and did so despite the stock market crash in October of the same year. \par \par \uc2  Baker said central banks today, individually and through the Basel Committee, should continue to ensure the 'efficiency, transparency and accountability of international financial markets.' \par \par \uc2  He warned against introducing capital controls in the face of crisis such as that seen in Mexico last winter. 'Any idea of introducing capital controls is not just unworkable, but unwise,' said Baker. \par \par \uc2  Baker emphasized that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market must be part of a broader effort and said it works best when 'going with - not against - the direction of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at the time.' \par \par \uc2  However, he stressed that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability can only be achieved through structural reform of the major economies, and noted that the structural trade surplus of Japan and the structural trade deficit in the U.S. continue to contribute to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instability as they did in 1985. Baker blamed the huge budget deficits of the advanced economies as well for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-10-95 \par \par \uc2  0902GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dran08650\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
