\par\par \b \uc2  G-7: Tietmeyer/Dlr -4: Reiterates Caution On  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1995\par 17:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Meantime, Tietmeyer strongly reiterated the Bundesbank's position that concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  can only be successfully exercised infrequently and only under the right circumstances. \par \par \uc2  '\b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are, in certain limited situations, completely useful,' Tietmeyer said. But he quickly added that fiscal and monetary policies also have to be going in the right direction to have a lasting impact. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  can only take place after markets have begun taking the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend in the right direction to begin with. He said the highly successful concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks from the U.S., \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Germany back in August had been conducted under the right circumstances. \par \par \uc2  Tietmeyer stressed that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, cannot fundamentally change the direction of a major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on their own. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, they merely serve as a strong signal to the markets in accompaniment to basic policy measures (such as budgetary consolidation) that governments must take. Germany, the U.S. and the rest of the Group of seven (G-7) industrial countries agree on that, Tietmeyer asserted. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-10-95 \par \par \uc2  1529GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dra707t