\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Higher After Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 1995\par 02:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--The dollar is higher in early Tokyo trading Friday than its levels late in New York Thursday, after a round of aggressive dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  put a firm bottom under the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 99.80 yen shortly after 0001 GMT. Traders said that triggered stop-loss buying orders from interbanks, who are seen unwilling to go aggressively short the dollar ahead of the Group of Seven (G-7) summit Saturday, traders say. \par \par \uc2  Position squaring on the eve of the G-7 summit to be held in Washington led U.S. funds to sell dollars for yen late Thursday, traders say, but the BOJ was unwilling to let the dollar fall below far below 100.00 yen. Traders said the BOJ has placed major dollar-buy orders at 99.80 yen with Japanese banks. \par \par \uc2  Around 0030 GMT, the dollar is trading at 100.13 yen, up from 99.80 yen around 0001 GMT and above 99.40 yen in New York late Thursday. The dollar was quoted at 100.55 yen late in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at 1.4245 Deutsche marks, higher than 1.4225 marks around 0001 GMT and above 1.4190 marks late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at 1.4335 marks in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at 70.29 yen, up from 70.16 yen around 0001 GMT and above 70.05 yen in New York late Thursday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Thursday at 70.14 yen. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.5847, up from $1.5845 around 0001 GMT but below $1.5860 in New York late Thursday. Sterling was at $1.5871 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-10-95 \par \par \uc2  0039GMT \par \par \uc2  1046 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dra607sua\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
