\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar tumbles despite Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tsukasa Maekawa \par \uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 29 (Reuter) - The sagging dollar suffered another blow on Friday, plunging below 98 yen as Japanese exporters sold dollars to settle accounts on the final business day of the first half of the fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted the greenback off its lows with dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in morning trade, but was forced to step in again after the fragile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell back. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was hovering around 98 yen and 1.4170 marks in late afternoon trade after closing at around 99.25 yen and 1.4190 marks in New York on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The yen's surge against the dollar battered Tokyo share prices. The key Nikkei average ended down 109.80 points at 17,913.06. \par \par \uc2  A finance ministry official sought to sooth \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters, calling the dollar's drop a technical move and insisting the Group of Seven (G7) leading nations would reaffirm their commitment to a strong dollar when their finance ministers and central bankers meet in early October. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Prime Minister Tomiichi Murayama told parliament he would do his best to ensure Japan's economy recovered and would keep a "close watch" on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen's renewed rise is bad news for Japan's stagnant economy, as it could dent exporters' profits. \par \par \uc2  The government last week announced a mammoth 14.22 trillion yen ($145 billion) package of economic stimulus measures in an attempt to put the economy back on a recovery track. \par \par \uc2  The cabinet approved an extra budget worth 5.325 trillion yen ($54.3 billion) on Friday to partially finance the package. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the Bank of Japan bought dollars around 97.50 yen and above in Tokyo morning trade, after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as low as 97.45 yen earlier in the morning. \par \par \uc2  The dollar recovered a bit, only to retreat again in late afternoon, when the Bank of Japan again came into the market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which touched a record low of 79.75 yen in April, hit a 15-month high of 104.70 yen last week. It had been hovering between 98 yen and 101 yen since. \par \par \uc2  Sales of dollars to buy marks helped push the dollar lower, along with selling by U.S. funds to buy yen. Japanese exporters also bought the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to book their overseas earnings on the last business day of the fiscal half-year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was half-hearted at best and no match for the aggressive selling, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers predicted the dollar would remain fragile and under pressure at least until the G7 ministers' meeting, which is expected around the first week of October. \par \par \uc2  Some said that since the dollar's rise earlier in September was an artifical creation of G7 authorities, it would be hard to reverse its latest weakening without another dose of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr9t03jc6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
