\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Japan/Branch Managers -2: First Since Sept. 8 Ease \b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1995\par 07:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--The Bank of Japan announced Friday that it will hold its next quarterly meeting of its branch managers at its headquarters in Tokyo Oct. 23 and 24. \par \par \uc2  The branch managers' meeting will be the first since the Bank of Japan on Sept. 8 cut its official discount rate by 0.5 percentage point to the new post-World War II record low of 0.5% per annum. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that time said and has since maintained that the stagnation in the economy is continuing and that there are concerns that the pause in economic recovery may be prolonged. \par \par \uc2  The scheduling of the meeting comes as Japanese financial markets, rocked in part by concerns about the stability of Japan's financial system, have been fairly volatile. On Friday, the dollar tumbled 2 yen during the Tokyo morning to about 97.50 yen before Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recover to the mid-98-yen level by the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-09-95 \par \par \uc2  0516GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9t07kc1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
