\par\par \b \uc2  Japan's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  raises roller-coaster dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Linda Sieg \par \uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 22 (Reuter) - The dollar's roller-coaster ride swept upwards on Friday, with the greenback rebounding above 100 yen after aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  repaired heavy damage suffered in New York overnight. \par \par \uc2  Japanese economic mandarins, meanwhile, did their best to talk up the dollar, defending Tokyo's latest economic stimulus package and blaming much of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp slide this week on factors in the United States and Europe. \par \par \uc2  "We (the Group of Seven nations) are seeking the orderly reversal of the dollar. (Japan) will take a bold stance in fighting any speculation that deviates from economic fundamentals," Finance Minister Masayoshi Takemura told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  He said the dollar's slide in London and New York was triggered mainly by worries over the future of Europe's monetary union. \par \par \uc2  "As for Japan's economic policy, I believe it has been uniformly appreciated at home and abroad and there is no sense of disappointment," Takemura said. \par \par \uc2  Economic Planning Agency Minister Isamu Miyazaki told a separate news conference that the dollar's latest fall -- which took it from a 15-month high of 104.70 yen on Wednesday to as low as 97.10 yen on Thursday -- was due mostly to U.S. factors including a widening American trade deficit. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's rise against the dollar has been caused by the U.S. situation," Miyazaki said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at around 100.65 yen at midday in Tokyo, boosted by repeated heavy dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  One dealer estimated that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent between $7 billion and $10 billion to bolster the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffered its biggest one-day loss against the yen in 20 months in New York on Thursday, falling as low as 97.10 yen as neither the U.S. Federal Reserve nor Germany's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to defend it. \par \par \uc2  It closed in New York at around 99.15 yen. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan had entered the market in Tokyo trade on Thursday, but traders called its purchases anaemic. \par \par \uc2  Dealers blamed several factors for the dollar's latest slide, including worries over European monetary union, concern over the U.S. trade and budget deficits, and the absence of U.S. and German dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Thursday sell-off accelerated a dollar drop that began on Wednesday, when markets showed their disappointment over Japan's latest economic stimulus package and the failure of the Bank of Japan to step into the market in a big way. \par \par \uc2  The $136 billion economic package was Japan's biggest-ever spending binge aimed at kick-starting its stalled economy, but failed to address key problems such as financial institutions' huge bad debts, tax reform and deregulation. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment towards the greenback remained frail, although some dealers said the sharp drop was a natural correction and would likely be followed eventually by further gains. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers, however, said they had lost confidence in authorities' ability to maintain the momentum behind its stunning rise from an April record low of 79.75 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Since it was \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities' efforts that bolstered the yen above 100 yen, it was an artificial creation. With confidence in the authorities betrayed, there was a big counter-reaction," said a Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr9m03sh7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
