\par\par \b \uc2  Japan/Markets/Package-3: Domestic Demand Boost May Help Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 1995\par 06:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Other sectors in the stock market may still enjoy benefits from the package, however. Construction and telecommunications stocks, which have recently run up on expectations for more domestic demand-related spending, could continue to stay strong as investors search for alternatives to recently popular high technology issues, says Keiji Ikeda at BZW Securities (Japan) Ltd. \par \par \uc2  Over the longer term, the economic package's impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market could help the dollar move higher against the yen if it provides a lift to the Japanese economy, market players say. Hill at S.G. Warburg says new spending by the government will stimulate domestic demand and make it easier for foreign goods to enter Japan, thereby boosting the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has since dipped to its lowest levels of the day in Tokyo, trading at 104.00 yen around 0420 GMT. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars around 104.00 yen after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was sold off on profit-taking earlier Wednesday, and market participants are continuing to keep an eye out for further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the package's effect on the bond market is uncertain, stategists say, because it is unclear how much money will be raised by issuing bonds, and whether those bonds would be issued directly to the market or whether some would be allocated to government arms, such as the Trust Fund Bureau. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Takemura said at his press conference that about 200 billion yen in deficit finance bonds would be issued to pay for the package. Government sources also told AP-Dow Jones late Tuesday that government bond and regional bond issuance to finance the package would total around 8 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-09-95 \par \par \uc2  0433GMT \par \par \uc2  1138 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9k07bpj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
