\par\par \b \uc2  Global  \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange \highlight\uc2  turnover tops trillion dollars a day. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Phil Smith \par \uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 19 (Reuter) - Trading on the world's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets has ballooned in the past few years and now tops a trillion dollars per day, the latest survey by central banks showed on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  London retained the top position as the world's leading \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  centre with New York second and Tokyo still third. Central banks across the world made their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  findings available for the tri-yearly survey of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity carried out by the Bank for International Settlements (BIS). \par \par \uc2  Recent years have seen a big rise in speculative activity on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and has also witnessed the rise of the so-called hedge funds such as the Quantum fund run by Hungarian-born financier George Soros. \par \par \uc2  Soros was said to have made a billion dollars by speculating against the pound during the sterling crisis in 1992 but the Bank of England said the rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity did not indicate an increase in speculative activity. \par \par \uc2  "I don't believe there's anything here that you can draw on to reach any conclusion as to whether any of this reflects a heightened level of speculative activity," Bank of England director Ian Plenderleith told reporters when the British \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  published its findings. \par \par \uc2  Around 25 central banks are taking part in the survey and the BIS will produce an analysis of the size of the global \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market early next year. \par \par \uc2  The survey was carried out during April so the Tokyo turnover figures may be distorted by the huge \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it was trying in vain to rein in the soaring yen. \par \par \uc2  On a net basis, with data adjusted for double counting, London stood out with a 60 percent leap in turnover to $464 billion with New York second, up 46 percent to $244 billion. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo hung on to third place despite some speculation that Singapore would nose ahead this time. Tokyo saw volume rise 34.3 percent to $161.4 billion with Singapore up 43.2 percent to $105.4. \par \par \uc2  The previous survey from 1992 estimated global net turnover at some $880 billion every business day in April of that year, a 42 percent rise from the $620 billion in April 1989. \par \par \uc2  These reports however are limited to figures for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactons in spot, outright forward and swaps and exclude transactions in futures and options. Findings on these will be published separately from the main report. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of England noted the massive rise of swap trading since the last survey. \par \par \uc2  It said nearly 80 percent of the rise in total turnover in London since 1992 was due to the rise in activity in the swap market due to the increasing use of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to hedge \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk and manage liquidity. A \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap is a simultaneous purchase and sale, or vice versa, of identical amounts of one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for another with two different value dates, normally spot to forward. \par \par \uc2  Others major centres reporting on Tuesday included, Switzerland, with turnover up 30 percent, Hong Kong, up almost 50 percent, Germany, up 40 percent, and Canada up 36 percent. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr9j03wm1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
