\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Survey -3: Particularly Active In April 1995 \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 1995\par 17:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Foreign banks increased their share both in interbank trading and in customer transactions. \par \par \uc2  Foreign interbank deals increased to 55% in April 1995 from 47% in April 1992, while foreign banks' customer transactions increased to 31% from 22%. The Bank of Japan also noted the proportion of transactions conducted through brokers in the interbank market declined to 28% from 37%. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan official noted that electronic broking constituted 12% of interbank brokerage transactions in April 1995, compared with nil in 1992. He noted that this share is likely to continue increasing. \par \par \uc2  In response to a reporter's question whether as to the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses electronic broking for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  official noted news reports to that effect but said he couldn't comment. \par \par \uc2  He also said the aggregate data for turnover 'of course' include Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the survey includes all participants in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in Tokyo. Although the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't disclose any details of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's activity is reflected in the nation's foreign reserves figures. \par \par \uc2  In April 1995, Japan's foreign reserves, including convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund (IMF) special drawing rights, surged $12.15 billion from March to $153.67 billion for the second-largest rise ever. \par \par \uc2  The official added that yen trading in April was particularly active. On April 19, the dollar hit an historic low of 79.85 yen, and turnover was heavy in the month. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-09-95 \par \par \uc2  1508GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9j078sy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
