\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Surges To 14-Month High Against Yen: World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By CAROLINE HUMER \par \uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1995\par 22:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (AP-DJ)--The dollar rallied Wednesday to hit a new high for the year against the yen, as well as the highest level in 14 months. The move was sparked by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the belief that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's large companies are also investing in the dollar at these levels. \par \par \uc2  The dollar reached a high of 102.75 yen at 1751 GMT. The last time it traded higher was June 17, 1994, when it hit 103.72 yen. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar continued to push higher on the back of good purchases by Japanese life insurers out of Japan into dollars and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said John McCarthy, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ING Capital Markets Inc. in New York. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's gains against the yen finally helped drag the dollar up against the Deutsche mark to the highest levels reached since Aug. 24, the date on which the Bundesbank cut its discount rate to 3.50% from 4.00%. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit an intraday high of 1.4975 marks at 1806 GMT. On Aug. 24, it traded at 1.4986 marks. \par \par \uc2  The mark lost ground Wednesday after the Bundesbank eased its securities repurchase rate in line with market expectations to 4.15% from 4.20%. Some took this as a signal the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would eventually lower its discount rate from its current level of 3.50%. The repo rate is expected to fall to 4.00% in the next few weeks. \par \par \uc2  The securities repurchase, or repo, rate is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key instrument for managing the money market. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was quoted at 1.4937 marks, up from 1.4733 marks late Tuesday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also quoted at 102.75 yen, up from 101.10 yen. Sterling was trading at $1.5487, down from $1.5560. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-09-95 \par \par \uc2  2018GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9d074b2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
