\par\par \b \uc2  (AWSJ): Japan Discount-Rate Cut Signals Attack On Slump \b0\par\par\uc2  By JATHON SAPSFORD and ROBERT STEINER \par \uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 1995\par 02:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--Japan's surprise discount-rate cut is the strongest sign yet of the government's new aggressiveness in tackling the country's economic ills. \par \par \uc2  But doubts remain that the move can restore confidence in the economy. Shortly after the Bank of Japan cut the rate Friday, it released a comprehensive survey showing that sentiment among Japanese corporate managers took a decided turn for the worse in August, Monday's Asian Wall Street Journal reports. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed the discount rate by half a percentage point to an unprecedented low of 0.5%, an aggressive step that surprised even officials at other government agencies. 'I was expecting only a quarter-point cut,' said an official at the Finance Ministry. \par \par \uc2  The action caps a series of moves by the Japanese government to shore up the country's business prospects. In recent weeks, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bureaucrats moved quickly to stanch bank runs and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to rein in the damaging effect of the strong yen on Japan's export industries. \par \par \uc2  The government will stoke the economy further this month with the release of a large stimulus package and a new support plan for a financial system burdened by bad debts. \par \par \uc2  'Since August, the government has been moving in advance of economic developments rather than lagging them,' said Hidetoshi Tsuchiya, senior economist at Sanwa Research Institute. \par \par \uc2  But while the government strives to put Japan on the road to recovery from its longest and deepest economic downturn in postwar history, business leaders weren't exactly ebullient Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-09-95 \par \par \uc2  0011GMT \par \par \uc2  1121 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9b06yv3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
