\par\par \b \uc2  Japan slashes key interest rate to bolster economy. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Linda Sieg \par \uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Reuter) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed its key lending rate by half Friday to an historic low of 0.5 percent to bolster the country's flagging economy and give relief to its fragile banking system. \par \par \uc2  The move, backed by aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sent the dollar leaping briefly above the 100 yen level for the first time since January and sent Tokyo stock prices soaring nearly 4 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which last cut its discount rate in April to the previous record low of 1 percent, said it was twinning the cut with a move to guide short-term market rates lower by providing ample funds to the money market. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan expects these decisions will lead to a further decline in interest rates across the board, thereby contributing to a steady recovery in the economy with price stability," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masayoshi Takemura also said the rate cut would help the economy, which has been trapped at near zero growth for nearly four years. \par \par \uc2  "The discount rate cut will help wipe out uncertainties over the future economy and ensure Japan's economic recovery," Takemura told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  Clearly, the uncertainties are great. \par \par \uc2  A Bank of Japan survey, released after the rate cut was announced, showed corporate executives became gloomier about business prospects in August despite a weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  A key component of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's survey, the diffusion index for major manufacturers, fell to minus 18 in August from minus 16 in May, when the survey was last conducted. It was the first time companies' outlook had worsened since November 1993. \par \par \uc2  The index, which compares the number of firms expecting business to get worse with those expecting improvement, is expected to stay at minus 18 in the next survey in November. \par \par \uc2  Japanese big business applauded the rate cut, as did U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin in Washington. \par \par \uc2  Moving quickly after the rate cut, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  whipped the dollar higher with aggressive dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ's (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) aggressive dollar buying was almost scary today. It seemed quite determined to drive the dollar up above 100 yen," said a European bank trader. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed unable to hold the 100 yen level for long in Tokyo as massive profit-taking set in. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the cut in the key rate, at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lends to private banks, would help get the economy back on track and give some relief to financial firms staggering under heaps of bad debt inherited from the collapse of asset prices in the early 1990s. \par \par \uc2  "On the monetary side we have a full commitment to reflate -- these are decisive steps to try to kick-start the economy," said Jesper Koll, chief economist at JP Morgan in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  But the credit easing will hardly solve all of Japan's economic problems, many of which are structural rather than merely the result of a cyclical downturn, economists said. \par \par \uc2  "It's necessary but not sufficient," said Chris Calderwood, an economist at Barclays de Zoete Wedd in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Lower rates need to be backed by hefty government spending to boost domestic demand and by deregulation to cut the red tape that strangles enterprise, economists said. \par \par \uc2  "We have to see how they perform on the fiscal side and see whether we get similar decisive measures," said Koll. \par \par \uc2  Japanese leaders have pledged to unveil around Sept. 20 a package of steps to stimulate the economy, to be backed by a hefty extra budget for the fiscal year ending March 31. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan Governor Yasuo Matsushita told a news conference the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take appropriate monetary steps in the future, if needed, but economists said the rate cut -- the ninth since 1991 -- could well be the last. \par \par \uc2  "Until it gets down to zero, it's hard to be emphatic, but certainly when the rate is so low there is a much better prospect that it's the last cut," BZW's Calderwood said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr9804443\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
