\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Treasurys In Tokyo Mostly Up On BOJ Rate Cut, Dlr Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 1995\par 09:24\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--Prices of U.S. Treasurys in Tokyo were mostly higher late Friday amid the dollar's surge following the cut in the Bank of Japan's discount rate. \par \par \uc2  Wholesale selling when the dollar hit above 100 yen was countered by strong individual buying across the yield curve, a senior trader at a medium-sized Japanese securities firm says. \par \par \uc2  While the dollar's surge was seen generally favorable for Treasurys, some traders expressed doubt that it would have a lasting impact on the market. 6    %   2-year 100 11/32   Up  1/32  5.81% 6 1/4%   5-year 100 31/32   Unchanged 6.02 6 1/2%  10-year 102  2/32   Up  1/32  6.22 6 7/8%  30-year 103 21/32   Up  5/32  6.59 2-30-yr yield spread: 78 bps vs 80 bps \par \par \uc2  As reported, at 0300 GMT the Bank of Japan cut its discount rate by 0.5 percentage point to the record low 0.50%. Almost immediately afterward, with market conditions thin during the local lunch hour, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  began aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the dollar. \par \par \uc2  As fears of possible joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  later Friday also buoyed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar hit an intraday high of 100.02 yen at 0517 GMT - its first rise above 100 yen since Jan. 23. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading 99.90 yen, up from 98.98 yen in New York late Thursday and above 98.65 yen late in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  With the Bank of Japan's rate cut Friday, market focus was seen shifting to whether the Federal Reserve will follow with an easing near-term, a trader with a large Japanese commercial bank says. Earlier this week, U.S. reports said the Fed will wail until congress settles the budget hits autumn before acting on interest rates. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 09-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0324EDT \par \par \uc2  4035 4041 4077 4085 4118 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024dr98022eo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
