\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Down Late In Asia; Support Seen Firm On BOJ Fear \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 1995\par 07:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (DJTES)--The dollar is lower in Tokyo trading late Thursday compared with its levels in New York late Wednesday, although traders expect the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain well supported around current levels on fears that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  'Basically, nervousness about Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and talk of a possible cut in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official discount rate (ODR) are supporting the dollar,' said Satoshi Inoue, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Bank of Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Around 0537 GMT, the dollar is quoted at 98.65 yen, below 98.83 yen late Wednesday in New York and lower from 98.78 yen late Wednesday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is quoted at 1.4755 Deutsche marks, lower than 1.4768 marks late Wednesday in New York and below 1.4785 marks in London Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there are growing expectations that the Bank of Japan will cut the ODR to 0.5% from the current 1.0% to ease concern about the banking system, which is laden with bad debt problems, to further weaken the yen and to jump-start the flagging economy. \par \par \uc2  Most traders said, however, that such a move likely will be timed to give an added boost to an economic stimulus package set for release Sept. 20. \par \par \uc2  'No cuts until Sept. 20,' said a Tokyo-based trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-09-95 \par \par \uc2  0538GMT \par \par \uc2  28038 \par \par \uc2 