\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Down Midday In Asia; BOC Said Selling Dlr-Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 230 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 1995\par 04:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (DJTES)--The dollar is weaker at midday in Tokyo Thursday than its levels early in the session, on profit-taking selling by speculators amid talk of the Bank of China being an active player. \par \par \uc2  The head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a major Japanese commercial bank said it's likely that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar-yen buying should the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fall below 98.50 yen in the remaining hours of the Asian trading day. \par \par \uc2  The chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Japanese long-term credit bank said the Bank of China was seen selling dollars just above 99.00 yen early in the day, but that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since then been rumored to have bought around 98.50/60 yen. \par \par \uc2  Around 0205 GMT, the dollar is trading at 98.70 yen, down from 98.91 yen around 0030 GMT and below 98.83 yen in New York late Wednesday. The dollar was quoted at 98.88 yen in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at 1.4770 Deutsche marks, lower than 1.4822 marks earlier in Tokyo and below 1.4768 marks late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at 1.4700 marks in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-09-95 \par \par \uc2  0206GMT \par \par \uc2  28038 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9706v9i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
