\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Soars On Japanese Buying, German Repo Cut: World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By CAROLINE HUMER \par \uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 1995\par 22:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (AP-DJ)--Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a larger-than-expected lowering in the German securities repurchase rate helped send the dollar sharply higher. \par \par \uc2  After the release of Japan's July current account surplus, which fell 21% from the year-earlier month to $9.22 billion, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and drove up the dollar near its intraday high of 99.20 yen. \par \par \uc2  The current account balance is the difference between the nation's income from foreign sources and foreign obligations payable excluding net capital investment. \par \par \uc2  Just as the effect on the dollar of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was starting to wane, the Deutsche Bundesbank allowed its securities repurchase rate to be lowered by 0.10 percentage point to 4.20%. The repo rate is the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's favorite tool for determining money market rates. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was successful and the rate cut was a little larger than expected,' said Paul Farrell, managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Chase Manhattan Corp. \par \par \uc2  The two factors together led the market to look for further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as U.S. trading began, Farrell said, pointing out the similarities to the last coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Aug. 15, the central banks of the U.S., Germany, Japan and Switzerland bought dollars, with the Bank of Japan buying dollars early in the day after the release of Japan-U.S. trade surplus numbers that had been favorable for the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was quoted at 1.4768 Deutsche marks, up from 1.4615 marks late Tuesday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also at 98.82 yen, up from 97.50 yen. Sterling was trading at $1.5510, down from $1.5590. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-09-95 \par \par \uc2  2039GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9606v1k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
