\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Fed Rate Cuts Taking Back Seat To Budget \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 1995\par 23:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Whether or not the Fed cuts short-term rates may not have as large an effect on the dollar as some believe. Analysts generally agree that cutting rates hurts the dollar by making investment in the U.S. and its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  less attractive. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading is focusing on U.S. economic growth and how the government handles that growth, according to Mark Gargano, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at First Union Bank of North Carolina. \par \par \uc2  Gargano pointed to a slew of U.S. economic data released Friday. The government reported that U.S. non-farm payrolls increased, but that much of the employment gains came in the service sector. In addition, statistics from the National Association of Purchasing Management indicated the U.S. manufacturing sector is showing some very weak signs. \par \par \uc2  With the current trend of consolidation in many important industries in the U.S., such as banking, Gargano said he sees unemployment rising. With the signs of a slow economy, the U.S. will have a harder time achieving the spending cuts sought by some conservative members of Congress. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. budget needs to be approved by Oct. 1, the beginning of fiscal 1996. Partisan politics have been holding up budget deliberations. \par \par \uc2  'If the U.S. does make some good inroads and still appears to be going ahead with the spending cuts, then the dollar will rise,' said Gargano. If not, the dollar will suffer, particularly against the mark, he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which has been able to hold on to its recent gains against the troubled Japanese yen, hasn't been as strong against the mark, analysts noted. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hasn't had the advantage of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has reportedly kept the dollar up against the yen. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-09-95 \par \par \uc2  2136GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9506tm8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
