\par\par \b \uc2  Central banks launch dollar into orbit. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrew Young \par \uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 15 (Reuter) - The dollar soared against the mark and yen in Europe after concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caught an already bullish market by surprise. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the inclusion of the Bundesbank in the dollar buying spree was probably the main trigger for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ascent. The last time the Bundesbank, Federal Reserve and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  together was on May 31. \par \par \uc2  "This will reassure investors that the Bundesbank does want to see the dollar higher," said Malcolm Barr, an economist at Chemical Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "There was some caution among investors that the Bundesbank actually didn't want to see the mark weaken against the dollar, and that should have been removed now," said Barr. \par \par \uc2  By 1320 GMT the dollar had strengthened to 1.4770/80 marks and 96.72/82 yen from around 1.4500 and 95.00 just ahead of the concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It finished Monday's European session at 1.4360 and 93.55/65. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss National Bank also joined the fray, buying dollars for Swiss francs, and helping to boost the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in what had been fairly quiet, illiquid markets in the absence of much of continental Europe for national holidays. \par \par \uc2  "They can get double the bang for their buck by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  this afternoon. They have shown at the moment that they know when to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and when to get most value for money," David Coleman, chief economist at Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce, told Reuters Financial Television. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had started the day on a bright note anyway after news of a smaller than expected Japanese trade surplus for July helped support the BoJ's overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overall customs-cleared trade surplus shrank to $9.43 billion from $12.25 a year earlier. The much-watched surplus with the U.S. narrowed to $3.87 from $5.62 billion. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped lift the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its highest level against the mark since February 22 and. It has not been this strong against the yen since March 2. \par \par \uc2  Adrian Cunningham, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at UBS here, said, "The Buba came in this time because the dollar was trending stronger anyway. It probably confirms that there was some sort of covert agreement made at (April) G7." \par \par \uc2  He said that after the latest dollar surge a little profit-taking would probably emerge but noted players would be reluctant to hold short positions after recent bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have caught the market on the hop. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese government ignited the current rally when it announced a package to encourage overseas investment by Japan's institutions on August 2, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Recurrent bouts of dollar buying by the Bank of Japan since then have fuelled the move by sending a powerful message to the market that the authorities are serious about weakening the yen. \par \par \uc2  Chartists said the break of a five-year down trendline plotted at anywhere between 94.50-95.50 yen should open the way for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to test 100 yen. The trendline, stretching back to an April 1990 high of 160.35, has followed dollar/yen's decline and repelled the dollar four times since it started. \par \par \uc2  The release of slightly stronger than expected U.S. economic data was largely overshadowed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  July industrial output rose 0.1 percent against forecasts for a 0.2 percent decline. Capacity use stood at 83.4 percent versus forecasts for 83.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  --London newsroom - +44-171-324-6701 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr8f04ws9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
