\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Focus: BoJ Faces Big Battle To Push Dollar Higher \b0\par\par\uc2  By NICHOLAS HASTINGS \par \uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1995\par 09:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LONDON (AP-DJ)--The Bank of Japan is making its intentions very clear - it wants the dollar to break above resistance at 94.40 yen and it wants the break now. \par \par \uc2  Some are confident the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will win. 'The effort that is being made in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very determined,' said Mark Fox, chief European strategist at Lehman Brothers International. \par \par \uc2  Others are considerably more skeptical about the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability. '\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone won't be enough to make it break through,' warned Stephen Hannah, head of research at IBJ International in London. \par \par \uc2  All eyes focused on the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Tuesday as it stepped up recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to help ensure that the dollar's rally doesn't stumble as it nears the five-year-old trend line. \par \par \uc2  The exercise won plaudits from all around. \par \par \uc2  Not only was it timed to take advantage of low turnover levels in Japan while many companies are off on their mid-summer o-bon holidays, it was launched just before the release of figures showing a further slide in Japan's trade surplus both with the U.S. and the rest of the world. \par \par \uc2  'It has consistently been very cleverly timed,' Fox said, referring to earlier \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts after the government announced measures to encourage overseas investment a few weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  The new data showed that the country's overall trade surplus declined 23% to $9.43 billion in July from $12.25 billion a year before. The July total, analysts said, was at least $1 billion below expectations. Japan's surplus with the U.S. also fell, to $3.87 billion in July from $5.62 billion. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0733GMT \par \par \uc2  1066 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8f067mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
