\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 /Dollar-2: Bundesbank Participation Seen Key \b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1995\par 16:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Although the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken part in past coordinated exercises to lift the dollar from its recent historic lows at 1.3440 Deutsche marks and 79.85 yen, it has often done so reluctantly because it has seen the efforts as futile. \par \par \uc2  When the Fed and the Bank of Japan last waded into the market on July 7, the Bundesbank was notable by its absence. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did manage to lift the dollar over 87.00 yen but the move was far from convincing. \par \par \uc2  At the time, a U.S. monetary source cautioned that markets shouldn't read too much into the absence of the Bundesbank, or other European central banks, adding that Europe was watching yen development closely. \par \par \uc2  U.S. officials say the series of Federal Reserve and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since early June have been a signal to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that the U.S. and Japanese governments agree on the need for a weakening of the yen. The Fed participation reflects U.S. concerns that the strong yen and the recent stock market weakness in Japan could push the Japanese economy into a severe recession - creating problems for the financial and banking sectors. \par \par \uc2  More concrete dollar support emerged with the recent Japanese government package of measures to encourage overseas investment. This, along with continued dollar purchases by the Bank of Japan, helped trigger a more broad based rally that took the dollar up to technical resistance at just over 94.40 yen. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also dragged up towards 1.4500 Deutsche marks. \par \par \uc2  As the dollar rally faltered early this week at what analysts said was a 5-year trend line, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  started to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively late in Tokyo Tuesday in anticipation of the release of Japanese trade figures for July, showing that the country's trade gap was shrinking faster than many expected. \par \par \uc2  With the capital flows already working in the dollar's direction, this shift in current account flows was all that is needed to help convince the market of a dollar recovery, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-08-95 \par \par \uc2  1450GMT \par \par \uc2  (Corrected 1504GMT) \par \par \uc2  1135 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8f066kc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
