\par\par \b \uc2  Nippon Life to stay flexible on US bond investment. \b0\par\par\uc2 162 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 3 (Reuter) - Nippon Life Insurance Co will continue to maintain its flexible stance on U.S. bond investment after Japan announced measures to promote overseas investment by Japanese investors, a company official said. \par \par \uc2  He said that the company is currently examining whether to change its dollar-buying levels after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged above 90 yen following Wednesday's joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Wednesday a package of measures to promote Japanese investment abroad, which included lifting a ban on non-yen loans by Japanese insurance companies. \par \par \uc2  "The environment has been set to buy dollars after the deregulation measure, which the industry has been anticipating," the official said. \par \par \uc2  In the April to June quarter, when the dollar was below 85 yen, the company purchased about 70 billion yen worth of U.S. bonds, the official said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr8305cfe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
