\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar outlook unclear despite U.S.-Japan resolve. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elaine Lies \par \uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 3 (Reuter) - Japan and the United States have shown fresh resolve to cooperate in boosting the dollar, but it is unclear whether teamwork alone will be enough to ensure a firm recovery in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. and Japan are both concerned about keeping the dollar from harm. But until (things) change a bit more, it will be very difficult for the dollar to gain substantially," said Yasuji Yamanaka, a chief dealer at the Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  "Until the dollar makes it at least to 93 yen, I wouldn't say that trends have turned around," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 90.45/50 yen in late afternoon Tokyo, pulled down from its overnight high of 91.25 by profit-taking but still buoyant after Japan announced steps to curb the yen, followed by joint U.S.-Japanese market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although the two countries have previously worked together to strengthen the dollar, most recently in joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on July 7, this time was different, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They cited Japan's announcement on Wednesday of steps removing barriers to public and private Japanese institutions' overseas investment and loans. \par \par \uc2  The deregulatory package, which included scrapping limits on insurers' participation in syndicated loans and on their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans to overseas borrowers, lifted the dollar above the key 90 yen resistance level during Asian time. \par \par \uc2  The gains were then extended in New York on Wednesday when the Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, joining Tokyo in buying dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  "(The governments) must have cooperated behind the scenes. If the U.S. hadn't done anything after the announcement of the Japanese package, it just would have been the same old (unsuccessful) pattern," said Yamanaka. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin hailed Japan's package as "removing impediments to the capital markets". \par \par \uc2  He noted that it was consistent with the April 25 Group of Seven communique, in which Britain, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan and the United States called for an orderly reversal of the dollar's decline. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masayoshi Takemura said in a late Wednesday statement that Japan will continue coordinating policies with other major nations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Separately, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Reuters on Thursday that the previous day's concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the United States demonstrated the consensus on orderly reversal is still intact. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo dealers agreed. "The spirit of coordinated action is, I think, sincere, otherwise the dollar would not have risen so much," said Takako Masai, a dealer at Toronto Dominion Bank. \par \par \uc2  But dealers warned that the impact of the Japanese package would depend on how much investment actually resulted. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of investment could eventually even lead to a reduction in Japan's trade surplus, which would also help the dollar firm. But the question is how much are people actually willing to invest?" said Kazuya Imai, a manager at Hokkaido Takushoku Bank. \par \par \uc2  A key test of Japanese investors' appetite for foreign assets comes next week, when $42.5 billion worth of U.S. Treasury bonds will be auctioned in a quarterly refunding. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr8305c81\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
