\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dlr Down;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Remain \b0\par\par\uc2  By DAVID JOLLY \par \uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1995\par 07:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--The dollar lost a little ground Thursday in Asia to profit taking on Wednesday's gains, but only after it topped out 91.20 yen - its highest level since March 14. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was bolstered by fear of more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity, evidenced by the fact that a rumor the Bank of Japan bought dollars around 90.60/70 yen in the Tokyo afternoon was enough to push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly up toward 91.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market still hasn't made up its mind about the longer term meaning of the Japanese government's yen-weakening package. The finance ministry's announcement of the measures, which are aimed at weakening the yen by encouraging investment in foreign assets, started the dollar's climb in Asian dealings Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the timing of the package combined with a healthy dose of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, has pushed the dollar up into a new trading range, at least for the time being. \par \par \uc2  'I'm bullish (on the dollar) for the short term anyway,' said a trader at a major Japanese bank. 'I'm not going to argue with central banks.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT, the dollar is quoted at 90.74 yen, below 90.95 yen late Wednesday in New York and down from 90.80 yen late Wednesday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at 1.3935 Deutsche marks, lower than 1.3975 marks late Wednesday in New York and below 1.3980 marks in London Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at 65.12 yen, up from 65.08 yen in New York late Wednesday and above 64.95 yen in London late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0533GMT \par \par \uc2  1046 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8305vyb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
