\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup-2: BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Talk Unconfirmed \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1995\par 08:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  But traders said the run on Cosmo had only a psychological impact on the market, and didn't engender any major yen selling. \par \par \uc2  The main impact was that 'it reminded people that there is considerable instability in the Japanese financial system right now,' said a trader for a major Japanese bank. 'Every week we get these reminders that there are a lot of banks out there with a lot of problems.' \par \par \uc2  Traders reported a rumor the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tokyo morning trading, but the talk couldn't be confirmed. Recently the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cloaked its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in secrecy, and is rumored to have narrowed its dollar-buying activities to only a few institutions to protect its activity. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market didn't react to comments in Tokyo by U.S. Undersecretary of Commerce Jeffrey Garten, who said Monday the U.S. hopes to launch a new framework with Japan for discussions of a broader range of trade issues. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in Asia, the Australian dollar managed to pierce U.S.$0.7400-level, topping out at U.S.$0.7402 around 0318 GMT. Traders said Aussie dollar was helped by better than expected trade data and Australian dollar-New Zealand dollar cross trading. \par \par \uc2  Australia's June seasonally adjusted current-account deficit was A$2.39 billion, down from A$2.85 billion a month earlier. \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT, the Australian dollar was quoted at U.S.$0.7394, up from U.S.$0.7358 late in Asia Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP