\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dlr Up On Continued BOJ Buying, Traders Say \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 1995\par 04:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--The dollar is stronger against the yen and the Deutsche mark at midday in Tokyo Monday than its levels earlier in the session, following rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar at around 88.00 yen at 0127 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was also seen buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen around 87.90-88.00 yen around 0040 GMT, lifting the dollar off an intraday low of 87.83 yen at 0038 GMT, traders said. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a major Japanese bank said it is likely that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to buy dollars to prevent the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from slipping below 88.00 yen in Asian dealings Monday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0200 GMT, the dollar is trading at 88.13 yen, up from 87.85 yen around 0030 GMT but below 88.49 yen in New York late Friday. The dollar was quoted at 88.65 yen in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at 1.3973 Deutsche marks, higher than 1.3848 marks earlier in Tokyo and above 1.3851 marks late Friday in New York. The dollar was at 1.3865 marks in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is at 63.07 yen, down from 63.44 yen earlier in Tokyo and below 63.89 yen in New York late Friday. The mark was quoted in Tokyo late Friday at 63.94 yen. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.5953, up from $1.5948 earlier in Tokyo and above $1.5940 in New York late Friday. Sterling was at $1.5950 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders say the dollar will fluctuate between 87.50-88.50 yen, and 1.3830-1.3880 marks in Asian dealings Monday. \par \par \uc2  But every time the dollar posts gains versus the yen, sellers step in to push it back again, traders said. \par \par \uc2  A spot dealer at a Japanese bank said the Bank of China was seen selling dollars in the low 88.00 yen range early Monday, while the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling at around 88.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  'Everyone except the BOJ is selling,' the Japanese bank trader added. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a U.S. bank said the upper half of 88.00 yen is regarded as top-heavy by speculators. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. bank trader said 87.50 yen is a critical support point for the dollar, adding that there is a considerable amount of sell orders of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that level placed by Japanese investors. \par \par \uc2  'Below 87.50 yen, the BOJ won't be able to keep the dollar afloat,' the trader said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-07-95 \par \par \uc2  0217GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7o05lwr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
