\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Mixed In Reaction to Japan Elections: World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By JOSEPH REBELLO \par \uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 1995\par 23:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (AP-DJ)--The dollar was mixed Monday, hurt by the uncertain outcome in Japanese elections Sunday but buoyed a little by renewed expectations for a German interest-rate cut. \par \par \uc2  The elections, which bloodied Japan's ruling coalition in the upper house of Parliament, wiped out much of the dollar's gains against the yen since the Bank of Japan started to push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  The result left traders fretting about whether the government would now be able to administer a quick remedy for Japan's ailing economy and its troubled banking sector. The yen, which by its strength has contributed to Japan's economic ills, strengthened after the elections. \par \par \uc2  'There's a perception that policy will remain a muddle, because no decisive ruling combination was found,' said Carl Weinberg, chief economist at High Frequency Economics in New York. 'And we don't think the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the dollar from sinking.' \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars repeatedly since July 7, when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the U.S. Federal Reserve to boost the dollar. Largely on the strength of the bank's moves, the dollar has inched upward against the yen since then. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was quoted at 1.3853 Deutsche marks, up from 1.3851 marks late Friday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also quoted at 87.45 yen, down from 88.49 yen. Sterling was trading at $1.5950, up from $1.5940. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-07-95 \par \par \uc2  2105GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7o05kxb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
