\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Mixed After Japanese Elections Late In Asia \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 1995\par 07:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (DJTES)--The dollar was mixed in Asian dealings Monday compared with its levels in New York late Friday, despite a sharp early fall in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that traders said was met by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also said to be in the market in the Tokyo afternoon, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar tumbled from an intraday high of 88.90 yen at 2359 GMT to a low of 87.83 yen in a span of only 39 minutes, despite active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the dollar by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market paid little attention to Japan's national elections Sunday, which saw Prime Minister Tomiichi Murayama's coalition government narrowly survive after his Social Democratic Party won only 16 of the 41 seats it entered with. Had Murayama's party won a few less seats, the government could have fallen, political analysts said. \par \par \uc2  'The election results were pretty much what people expected,' said Takemi Kaneko, general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Marubeni Corp. 'So there was no reason to buy or sell based on the results.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0540 GMT, the dollar is quoted at 88.30 yen, below 88.49 yen late Friday in New York and down from 88.55 yen late Friday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at 1.3870 Deutsche marks, higher than 1.3851 marks late Friday in New York and just below 1.3865 marks in London Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-07-95 \par \par \uc2  0543GMT \par \par \uc2  28038 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7o05g21\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
