\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday-2: BOJ Seen Unable To Boost Dlr Single-Handedly \b0\par\par\uc2 214 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1995\par 04:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A trader at a Japanese commercial bank said the dollar's fall against the mark in the wake of the decline in U.S. stocks and bonds Wednesday will make it difficult for the dollar to rebound against the yen. \par \par \uc2  He added that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ alone cannot push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up against the mark, although he acknowledged that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been making continuous efforts since early July to support the ailing dollar. \par \par \uc2  There have also been rumors Thursday morning that the U.S. Federal Reserve has been looking to buy dollars against the mark, but traders said they couldn't substantiate this speculation. \par \par \uc2  A Bank of Japan official Thursday morning declined to comment on U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  A European bank trader said the key issue for global trading Thursday is the dollar-mark range. He said dollar trading against the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is reflecting more accurately the decline in U.S. bonds and stocks following comments by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan which led market players to feel that rate cuts by the Fed have been put off. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-07-95 \par \par \uc2  0220GMT \par \par \uc2  1046 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7k05j4m\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdr